# spechub.conf — the one place that names your project, its repos and how to run them.
#
# `scripts/bootstrap.sh init <repos-root>` writes this file for you (stack detection);
# edit it by hand afterwards whenever a command, port or path is wrong. It is plain
# bash — every script in scripts/ sources it. Copy this example to spechub.conf.

PROJECT_NAME="My Platform"

# Base branch feature branches are cut from and merged back into (dev, develop, main …).
BASE_BRANCH="main"

# Push the base branch to origin after every Step 4 merge (1 = yes). The merge fast-forwards the local base
# to origin first and refuses to run if it has diverged; `dispatch.sh merge --no-push` keeps one merge local.
MERGE_PUSH="1"

# Headless coding agent that runs the prompts (WORKFLOW.md Step 3): claude | codex | copilot.
# AGENT_BIN overrides the PATH lookup.
AGENT_CLI="claude"
#AGENT_BIN=""

# Model per tier for that CLI. Prompts name a tier — Light (simple/backend/config work),
# Standard (moderate logic, light UI), Advanced (complex UI or reasoning) — and the dispatcher
# maps it here. Leave commented for the built-in defaults of the chosen CLI.
#MODEL_LIGHT=""
#MODEL_STANDARD=""
#MODEL_ADVANCED=""

# Parent directory of the service repos. Relative `dir` entries below resolve against it. A relative
# REPOS_ROOT resolves against this hub folder (e.g. ".." when the hub sits next to the repos), so a clone
# of the hub at the same place under another root finds that root's repos.
REPOS_ROOT="$HOME/projects/my-platform"

# Several instances of the whole stack on one machine (another folder, another checkout): each instance
# is its own root with its own hub, and its gitignored spechub.local.conf sets PORT_OFFSET (every port
# below + offset; `{port}` in a start command and the PORT env var get the shifted value) plus extra
# SERVICES rows such as its own database. `scripts/instance.sh init <new-root> <offset>` creates one;
# `scripts/instance.sh sync` brings an instance up to date before each workflow step.

# Gitignored files copied from a repo's main checkout into each fresh worktree so builds,
# tests and dev servers work there (glob patterns, space separated).
WORKTREE_COPY_FILES=".env .env.* application-local.properties"

# Dependency directories linked from the main checkout into each fresh worktree instead of
# reinstalling (only when they exist). Set DISPATCH_DEPS=install to reinstall instead.
WORKTREE_LINK_DIRS="node_modules .venv vendor"

# One line per runnable unit:  name|dir|start command|port|label|group|install command
#   name     short id used everywhere: service identifier in specs, prompts and scripts/stack.sh
#   dir      absolute, or relative to REPOS_ROOT — a git repo root, or a folder inside a monorepo
#            (worktrees are made of the git root; the service runs from the same folder inside them)
#   start    the dev-server command, run from `dir`. It must take its port from the PORT env var or
#            `{port}` (replaced by the effective port), or a PORT_OFFSET instance cannot move it
#   port     the port it listens on (used for status and collision checks)
#   label    human name shown on the board
#   group    static | backend | frontend — start order is static → backend → frontend
#   install  dependency install command run from `dir`, or - for none
# Order matters: it is the spec numbering order (01-, 02-, …) used by Step 0.
SERVICES="
web|my-monorepo/apps/web|npm run dev|3000|Web App (Next.js)|frontend|npm install
api|my-monorepo/apps/api|npm run start:dev|4000|Main API (NestJS)|backend|npm install
billing|my-billing|./mvnw spring-boot:run|8080|Billing Service (Spring Boot)|backend|./mvnw -q -DskipTests install
assets|my-billing/data|npx serve -l {port} --cors|3100|Asset server (serve)|static|-
"
